out written authorization from the pupil's parent or legal guardian\". That is rung 5: parental permission first.\n\n**Why it's blank:** a No vote rules out rung 5, but it doesn't tell rungs 1–4 apart. It can't show whether she wants parents told when they ask, schools to notify them, a ban on rules that make schools tell parents, or secrecy unless the student agrees. The vote wasn't near-unanimous, so that rule doesn't come into it. Both passages (the vote page and the bill text) are coded as one vote record. The fields are filled in as Part E requires.\n\n**One assumption:** her term dates are listed as unknown, so I coded the 2025 vote `in-term` on the assumption that she held the seat then. The tool that checks the labels against her service record will catch it if that's wrong.\n\n**`needs_source`:** her own words on telling parents, such as a statement, floor speech or questionnaire answer. Also any related bill she wrote or co-sponsored.\n\nNo quotes were coded, because neither source contains her own words.","ttft_ms":9260,"type":"result","duration_ms":25646,"uuid":"21431cef-c35a-4fdb-b885-88d4997f188e","ttft_stream_ms":1641,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":1642,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
